// Golden eval set — one JSON object per line. Blank lines and // comments are ignored.
//
// FIELDS
//   id                  short stable name, shown in `eval -verbose` output
//   query               the question, phrased the way a real user would
//   relevant_chunk_ids  chunk ids that genuinely answer it (from `chunks -dir`)
//   gold_answer         optional; enables citation + answer-correctness scoring
//   stage               optional; retrieval | rerank | generation — tags which
//                       stage the item exercises, so a regression can be
//                       attributed instead of merely observed
//   acl                 optional; permission tags to retrieve under
//
// Chunk ids are the contract. They change whenever chunking changes, so
// re-run `./ask-my-docs chunks -dir corpus` and update them after touching
// MAX_CHUNK_CHARS, CHUNK_OVERLAP, or the documents themselves.
//
// WHAT TO COVER — a set that only asks easy questions cannot detect anything:
//   - exact identifiers (error codes, SKUs, part numbers) — exercises the
//     sparse/lexical retrieval leg, which is what pure vector search gets wrong
//   - paraphrases sharing no words with the source — exercises the dense leg
//   - two chunks on the same topic where only one answers — exercises reranking
//   - questions your corpus genuinely cannot answer, with
//     "relevant_chunk_ids": [] — exercises the confidence gate. Without at
//     least one of these, `calibrate` cannot bound the gate from below.
//
// Aim for enough items that one flipping does not move the mean much. The 32
// items below put one item at 0.031, which is the floor `ablate` reports
// against — a difference smaller than that is not a finding.
//
// The items are grounded in the sample corpus/ shipped with this repo. On your
// own corpus they will all fail: replace them, do not adapt them.

// --- RestaurantIQ proposal ------------------------------------------------
// Short, densely sectioned prose. Exercises the dense leg — several of these
// share almost no vocabulary with the chunk that answers them.
{"id": "riq-stack-db", "query": "What database and cache does RestaurantIQ use?", "relevant_chunk_ids": ["RestaurantIQ_AI_Customer_Experience_Platform_Proposal.md#9"], "gold_answer": "PostgreSQL as the database and Redis as the cache.", "stage": "generation"}
{"id": "riq-stack-web", "query": "What frontend and backend frameworks does RestaurantIQ use?", "relevant_chunk_ids": ["RestaurantIQ_AI_Customer_Experience_Platform_Proposal.md#9"], "gold_answer": "Next.js/React on the frontend and FastAPI on the backend.", "stage": "generation"}
{"id": "riq-mvp-excluded", "query": "What is deliberately left out of the first release?", "relevant_chunk_ids": ["RestaurantIQ_AI_Customer_Experience_Platform_Proposal.md#5"], "gold_answer": "Custom NFC ordering, an employee portal, loyalty programs, marketing automation, POS integrations, an AI chatbot, advanced forecasting and enterprise workflows.", "stage": "generation"}
